1. Structural derivation - vLLM (Apache License 2.0)
   Copyright the vLLM Team.
   The transport-adapter interface and the outcome/metric shapes in this project
   are modeled on vLLM's serving benchmark, specifically the request-input,
   request-output, and request-function abstractions in
   vllm/benchmarks/lib/endpoint_request_func.py and the metric aggregation and
   goodput semantics in vllm/benchmarks/serve.py. The correspondence is at the
   level of interface shape and naming, deliberately, so that the result reads as
   native to a vLLM maintainer. No vLLM source is copied into this repository.
   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm

2. Methodology reference - NVIDIA Riva / Speech NIM (public documentation)
   Real-time-paced streaming with equal client and server chunk duration, three
   iterations per stream, and the fivefold-concatenation offline throughput cell
   follow NVIDIA's published ASR benchmark methodology so that results are
   comparable to their published tables. Referenced from public documentation and
   the public nvidia-riva/python-clients repository only.

